== Liability of the firm [Sec. 26] <26>
 
1. The wrongful act or omission of a partner, acting in the ordinary course of the business of a firm, or with the authority of his partners,
2. loss or injury is caused to any third party, or
3. any penalty is incurred.

The firm's liability flows to partners because the firm lacks independent legal personality—but partners are liable jointly and severally (individually) #ref(label("sec-25")), meaning creditors can pursue:
- The firm collectively, OR
- Any single partner for the FULL amount